        ],
        "year": 2023,
        "venue": "Workshop on Research Interfaces",
        "abstract": "Literature recommenders often hide missing abstracts, incomplete citation counts, and sampled candidate pools. We study uncertainty cues for recommendation lists and find that explicit missing-data labels help readers compare candidates without treating an ordering as a confidence score. We recommend separating provider rank from local text similarity.",
